  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A load of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math>&nbsp;falls from a height <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi></math> on the scale pan hung from a spring as shown. If the spring constant is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi></math> and the mass of the scale pan is zero and the mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> does not bounce relative to the pan, then the amplitude of vibration is&nbsp;</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0016_8f75afbfee6f.png\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 306px;\" /></p>"
  },
  "options": [
